{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/352543-how-much-is-that-unicorn-on-the-window-the-think-of-a-goblin-market-cost-thread","id":352543,"title":"\"How much is that unicorn on the window?\" (The Think Of A Goblin Market Cost Thread)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-28T04:51:47-08:00","id":352543,"title":"\"How much is that unicorn on the window?\" (The Think Of A Goblin Market Cost Thread)","content":"It's simple: say what you think the product in the previous post would probably cost in a Goblin Market, and leave e suggestion for a product. The following person does the same. By cost I mean what you pay up front to buy it and any potential side effects.<br /> <br /> I'll start: a straight up unicorn. It has the following characterisitcs:<br /> <br /> 1) Speech.<br /> 2) Levitation.<br /> 3) Two Masks: one of a man, and one of a normal horse.<br /> 4) All clauses of Eternal Summer, Eternal Spring, <a href=\"http://www.vtm.kismetrose.com/ctl/ContractChirurgery.html\" target=\"_blank\">Chirurgery</a>, Vainglory, Separation and Stone.<br /> 5) It is a True Fae Actor that was disconnected from its master and took on enough of its own identity to raise Wyrd without Titles. Its Wyrd is 7.<br /> 6) It belongs to the Fairest Seeming. It possesses the Draconic/Runnerswift/Chirurgeon Kiths.<br /> 7) A Fae Aspect that grants telekinesis.<br /> 8) The &quot;Immortal Flesh&quot; and the &quot;Ruled By Passion&quot; Fae Aspects. Virtue is Charity and Vice is Pride.<br /> 9) The Lethal Mien, Holistic Awareness and Faerie Healing Merits, plus any other Merits that you think would fit a unicorn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-28-2014, 08:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T02:22:54-08:00","id":358935,"title":"","content":"Who much for the Unicorn? The life you could have had if you chose to walk down a different path. (You must kidnap yourself from an alternate reality and sell that version of yourself to purchase the Unicorn from the Goblin Merchant.)<br /> <br /> Next up for auction: A bottle of liquid sunlight captured and stored away when the sun was born.(A vague curiosity indeed except when dealing with the cursed undead and Gentry who made Pledges to never be touched by the rays of the sun again.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T08:45:18-08:00","id":359167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/352543-how-much-is-that-unicorn-on-the-window-the-think-of-a-goblin-market-cost-thread?p=358935#post358935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who much for the Unicorn? The life you could have had if you chose to walk down a different path. (You must kidnap yourself from an alternate reality and sell that version of yourself to purchase the Unicorn from the Goblin Merchant.)<br /> <br /> Next up for auction: A bottle of liquid sunlight captured and stored away when the sun was born.(A vague curiosity indeed except when dealing with the cursed undead and Gentry who made Pledges to never be touched by the rays of the sun again.)</div> </div> </div> </div>To purchase the bottle of sunlight you must give up your ability to feel physically comfortable. In the heat, no amount of air conditioning or cool drink can cause you to feel anything but hot and sticky. In the cold, even the warmest fire cannot stave off the chill. Every bed is lumpy and every chair feels like sitting on the hard floor (-1 to rolls involving Resolve or Composure). This discomfort lasts until the sunlight in the bottle is all poured out, or a year and a day passes, whichever is longer.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> The Goblin merchant is selling a collection of 6 fresh, plump, seedless blueberries. He claims 5 of the 6 berries have miraculous healing properties when eaten (consuming one berry removes all damage from the rightmost health box with damage in it). The sixth gives the eater a brief glimpse of the future, but at a cost (the eater enters a catatonic state for one scene, but he gains the benefit of a vision of the future equivalent to the Omen three-dot contract &quot;Reading the Portents&quot;). It is impossible to tell which berries are which. What does the merchant ask in return for these berries?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://paizo.com/campaigns/RageAcrossIreland/gameplay\" target=\"_blank\">My W20 Play-by-Post Game</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2760-formosus","name":"Formosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T09:51:48-08:00","id":359247,"title":"","content":"Your hands. He wants <i>both</i> of them.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> How much do you think Your Beloved's Yesterday goes for? How about yours?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T17:18:49-08:00","id":359721,"title":"","content":"By Beloved's Yesterday? Goes for my single most cherished moment in time. My Yesterday? A single bag of popcorn that doesn't have any unpopped kernels. <br /> <br /> <br /> Oh, this next one's a real steal. One police grade pistol that has never been used for any purpose other than for good (A pistol that does aggravated damage to creatures without any form of Integrity score of one of 0 but at the cost that the attack roll will fail unless the Wyrd...caughSTORYTELLER..deems the act in the interest of universal good.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T17:36:36-08:00","id":359735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/352543-how-much-is-that-unicorn-on-the-window-the-think-of-a-goblin-market-cost-thread?p=359721#post359721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Oh, this next one's a real steal. One police grade pistol that has never been used for any purpose other than for good (A pistol that does aggravated damage to creatures without any form of Integrity score of one of 0 but at the cost that the attack roll will fail unless the Wyrd...caughSTORYTELLER..deems the act in the interest of universal good.)</div> </div> </div> </div>For this the Goblin Merchant wants the original copy of a signed and executed pardon for a murderer or other death row inmate who was <i>definitely guilty</i> of the crime was convicted of committing. The pardon can't be more than 10 years old.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <br /> A jar filled with orange bees sits on the shelf of the Merchant's stall. She claims that, if released, the bees will build a hive that produces a honey so sweet that it can be bartered to the True Fae in return for a captive, or to keep them from kidnapping the owner back to Arcadia.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://paizo.com/campaigns/RageAcrossIreland/gameplay\" target=\"_blank\">My W20 Play-by-Post Game</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2760-formosus","name":"Formosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T17:48:17-08:00","id":359746,"title":"","content":"The cost, obviously, is someone beloved that you feel fit to replace a captive you are bringing back. If not that? Someone you love dearly, and I mean <i>dearly</i>, who can take your place in Arcadia if the Gentry come a-knocking.<br /> <br /> Ooh, look at this: a pair of flesh-eating horses. Like the beasts of Greek legend, they will tear into anyone thrown at their feet, and are as swift as a lightning bolt and ferocious as a tiger. They feel no fear, and their hooves strike true whenever a briarwolf tries to snap at their heels. The only drawback is that they get stronger when they're hungry, and if left to starve, can literally break down walls to get a meal....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T18:07:22-08:00","id":359784,"title":"","content":"Flesh eating horses like from the Greek Mythg? I'll take em for a single box of Thin Mint Girlscout Cookies, or for a pair of canine teeth from an Elder Vampire from the Polis Erebus.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now what's this? An original copy of the House of Leaves...that serves as a portal to the actual growing rooms from the story? (A book that both serves as a map and unique key to a unique Hollow that may or may not be alive/inhabited by a horrific creature/cause those who come into contact with it to slowly lose Clarity.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T18:29:54-08:00","id":359796,"title":"","content":"I'll swap it for an ashcan copy of the Codex Seraphinianus, <i>with</i> the footnotes (if you know what I mean.)<br /> <br /> But here, my friend, I have an IOU for peace-of-mind from The Kindly Lady of Flowers; buy it, and anyone that tries to find you when you don't want to be found... well, they don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T02:14:06-08:00","id":360025,"title":"","content":"I'd say it'll go for the left sneaker of a 16 year old grandfather (Thanks you so very much time travel &amp; leap year.)<br /> <br /> Now how about this nifty trinket? A bathrobe that make it's wearer the desire of any and all onlookers. (While wearing the robe the person gains a combination of Fleeting Spring and Striking Looks.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spell check. 01-05-2015, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T05:22:07-08:00","id":361153,"title":"","content":"A copy of every single back issue of the Playboy magazine, in mint condition, sounds like a fair price.<br /> <br /> But see, here! I have here a bottle ofNothing! Special Nothing, that spreads wherever you pour it! A bargain at the price!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T12:43:12-08:00","id":361507,"title":"","content":"I'll trade it for my pet fox that's so cunning that none alive can track it...now if only I could remember where I left him. <br /> <br /> Ah, now this is a rare find! A plain old ordinary copper neckless with no supernatural qualities what so ever. Yes quite old and ordinary, just a present that was once given to an ordinary actress named Marilyn Monroe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T14:46:23-08:00","id":361616,"title":"","content":"$12.95 and some belly button lint... from the belly button of Lee Harvey Oswald.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Here we have an old bottle, empty of wine, nothing much to look at. The merchant claims it's a dream vessel containing the last earthly dream of an Exarch. What's an Exarch? Some big muckety muck witch or somethin', he's not exactly sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://paizo.com/campaigns/RageAcrossIreland/gameplay\" target=\"_blank\">My W20 Play-by-Post Game</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2760-formosus","name":"Formosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T15:00:36-08:00","id":361633,"title":"","content":"I'd buy that for a dollar, a specific dollar that has George Washington's eyes and the All Seeing Eye on the back all closed. As if they blinked when the artist was drawing their portrait.<br /> <br /> Next up, an iron key with the depiction of a weeping woman on the end. The Goblin Merchant claims that it can open any locked door, but where that unlocked door leads is anyone's guess. His words, not mine (A key that turns any door unlocked by it into a portal to...somewhere. Arcadia? The Underworld? Somewhere stranger? Only the Wyrd..STORYTELLEACHOH..&quot;sniff&quot; sorry about that, knows.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T16:42:58-08:00","id":361726,"title":"","content":"For the weeping woman key, the price is a doorknob taken from the front door of a Gentry's Hollow, while the Gentry is inside.<br /> <br /> Next up, a fishing rod that always catches a fish within one hour of being used. It also works as a sort of gambling device: you can use items of both monetary and emotional value as bait. As the value of the bait increases, so do the values of the rewards and probability of getting them. Example: with a ten dollar bill you have a 30% chance of getting boots, but with a 100 dollar bill you have a 90% chance of getting boots and a 10% chance of getting a gold ring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 01-06-2015, 07:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T16:51:59-08:00","id":361729,"title":"","content":"Cost: A pair of dice which have rolled thirteen snake-eyes followed by thirteen double-sixes in a row.<br /> <br /> A character sheet for a popular, alliteratively-titled fantasy roleplaying game. If filled out for a character as created out of the central corebook for that game, it generates a living facsimile of that character for day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T17:15:09-08:00","id":361760,"title":"","content":"(Seriously, HobbitGuy1420? That's way too expensive. I would make the cost something like a finger lost by a man who tried to force the reward out of a Hedge gambling machine.)<br /> <br /> For the D&amp;D character sheet, assuming it only works once and the conjured character is temporary, I would make the price your very imagination for 3 weeks (all rolls involving Intelligence/Wits for the purposes of solving problems and creating art are reduced to 1 die, but can be boosted with willpower).<br /> <br /> Next up, a pair of binoculars that can see through any barrier, magical or mundane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T17:28:24-08:00","id":361765,"title":"","content":"The cost for this item is a risqu\u00e9, nude picture of your mother, personally taken by yourself.<br /> <br /> You spot a pair of scissors made out of gold lying on the stall's counter. The hobgoblin by the antique register perks up and mentions the scissor can be used to cut through any kind of binding tied or otherwise secured by a fae creature (Changeling, True Fae, hob, it doesn't matter). He's unusually forthcoming, however, and says it's as useless as a spoon for cutting anything else.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://paizo.com/campaigns/RageAcrossIreland/gameplay\" target=\"_blank\">My W20 Play-by-Post Game</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2760-formosus","name":"Formosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T17:42:36-08:00","id":361787,"title":"","content":"For the gold scissors, I would make the price a pair of handcuffs used to arrest a serial killer with over 100 victims.<br /> <br /> Next up, an iron and leather mask that makes you completely immune to supernatural coercion, but makes you see the world filled with terrible hallucinations, requiring a Resolve + Composure roll divided by half round down every time it is activated to avoid gaining a temporary major derangement. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T18:40:41-08:00","id":361861,"title":"","content":"Easily for the cost of one mummified eye that once belonged to a man who never say anything that made sense in his life, and trough seeing gained enlightenment.<br /> <br /> I've got a nicknack for the ages, a pair of shoes that when out on phase it's wearer into Twilight (only works in the Mortal World.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T11:07:59-08:00","id":362700,"title":"","content":"For the Twilight shoes, I would make the price another pair of shoes, but they must have been worn by a person who walked from one end of the Hedge to the other.<br /> <br /> Next up, the Sibilant Sock: a white sock puppet with black buttons for eyes and black Hedge thorns for teeth. When worn on your hand, it takes on a life of its own and talks to you. It gives you great advice and listens to your problems, effectively acting as 3 dot Mentor, Common Sense and +1 on the next degeneration roll. However, it sometimes gives truly horrible advice, which the wearer will interpret as useful. Each time you use the Sibilant Sock, roll 1d10. If the result is a 1, you will automatically suffer a Dramatic Failure on a roll related to advice you asked for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T21:34:26-08:00","id":363194,"title":"","content":"((Really, all the dice would take would be a bit of time and maybe some Contract-based manipulation of things - but reduce the numbers to 7 or even 3 if you think it works better). <br /> <br /> For this sock, All that we ask is that you lend us your ear. - only we won't be giving it back. Only one ear, though. We're not crazy. <br /> <br /> Here we have an authentic hookah - which will also make the best Turkish coffee upon request, and can perfectly slice or dice any food placed beneath its bowl.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T21:43:04-08:00","id":363198,"title":"","content":"A lock of Gordon Ramsay's hair will do, sealed in an air-tight bag and sprinkled with sage.<br /> <br /> Now here's a poor, unfortunate soul: a completely-obedient werewolf, with shackles and chains and almost void of free will. Don't mind the drooling stare, or the giant scar in its forehead \u2014 poor thing was nearly lobotomized thanks to a silver axe. He'll rip something to pieces on command, or lift a car out of the way for you, but don't expect much in the way of conversation from him. He only says one thing too, over and over: <i>&quot;Arath...arath....&quot;</i> Suppose that's what you could call him, then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T00:28:28-08:00","id":363249,"title":"","content":"What a exquisite slave, I can think of but two thing that would be equal such a find: A kiss stolen from the Hungry Moon (beware this Noble Lady of Arcadia though, she's known to bite and never let go) or an ice cream sandwich that's kept at just the perfect temperature (Not to cold that the cookies get hard and not to warms so the ice team melts.)<br /> <br /> I doubt this next humble ware can trump the above find: A 45. Caliber Magnum that was actually blessed by an Angel, specifically an Angel of iron and steel who decreed that it's user rid his city of foul Demons (a Magnum that doubles as a Gadget from Demon: the Descent that allows it's wielded to activate the Hellfire Exploit at the cost of 1 Glamour since it's been in the Hedge long enought to corrupt the Gadget's occult mathematics.)<br /> <br /> (P.S. As a side note I'm so happy that this thread has taken off like it has. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":". 01-08-2015, 03:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T12:47:17-08:00","id":366552,"title":"","content":"The price is a kiss from a rose on a grave. Or a live seal. Getting either to the merchant is the trick.<br /> <br /> <br /> The next merchant has a large tome entitled &quot;For the Fairest.&quot; Now, calm down, you vainglorious ones: this has nothing to do with being pretty. The book is a universal guide to fairness. Every possible scenario is listed on the yellowing pages, alongside the response that the (unknown) author considered the most fair, by some arcane calculation.<br /> <br /> Not the morally correct response, not the response that would result in the greater good or satisfy justice. Just... &quot;Fair&quot;. A flick through shows that the fair response to a compliment on one's hair is a polite &quot;thank you&quot; and a similarly phrased compliment concerning the other party's shoes. The fairest price for a pair of handmade socks is a cheeseburger and a bag of blue marbles. The response to an enemy kidnapping your firstborn daughter is to torture their father with a heated blade for exactly nineteen hours and fourteen minutes.<br /> <br /> An odd item with an odd history: those who find it in their possession gradually lose the ability to deal with situations without referring to the book...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4722-birnam","name":"Birnam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T16:07:26-08:00","id":369108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Birnam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/352543-how-much-is-that-unicorn-on-the-window-the-think-of-a-goblin-market-cost-thread?p=366552#post366552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The price is a kiss from a rose on a grave. Or a live seal. Getting either to the merchant is the trick.<br /> <br /> <br /> The next merchant has a large tome entitled &quot;For the Fairest.&quot; Now, calm down, you vainglorious ones: this has nothing to do with being pretty. The book is a universal guide to fairness. Every possible scenario is listed on the yellowing pages, alongside the response that the (unknown) author considered the most fair, by some arcane calculation.<br /> <br /> Not the morally correct response, not the response that would result in the greater good or satisfy justice. Just... &quot;Fair&quot;. A flick through shows that the fair response to a compliment on one's hair is a polite &quot;thank you&quot; and a similarly phrased compliment concerning the other party's shoes. The fairest price for a pair of handmade socks is a cheeseburger and a bag of blue marbles. The response to an enemy kidnapping your firstborn daughter is to torture their father with a heated blade for exactly nineteen hours and fourteen minutes.<br /> <br /> An odd item with an odd history: those who find it in their possession gradually lose the ability to deal with situations without referring to the book...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Uncle Sam's trademark hat and britches (The hat of the anthropomorphic personification of the united states, not any one it might be based on) OR a hair from the head of one of the Exarchs (an Antigenator, not a lesser one)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The next item to the be sold is the concept of 7. The owner will have international trademark over the existance of a number between 6 and 8, and be well within his rights decide if a 7 is allowed to have that little extra line some people do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4190,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4190-nurseninja","user":"Nurseninja","date":". 01-13-2015, 07:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4190-nurseninja","name":"Nurseninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T18:34:24-08:00","id":369267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nurseninja;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The next item to the be sold is the concept of 7. The owner will have international trademark over the existance of a number between 6 and 8, and be well within his rights decide if a 7 is allowed to have that little extra line some people do.</div> </div> </div> </div> Obviously, you would need the handwritten signature of the person to first use Arabic Numerals, written in the year of 500 AD.<br /> <br /> This next object is truly potent. Legend says that, if given to any human or Changeling, they may, once in their lifetime, shatter it to ascend into a state of being far beyond their own, at which point, it will cease to exist for 1000 years before reforming. [In game terms, it allows normal mortals and Changelings to shuck whatever Supernatural abilities they have in order to Ascend into a Mage. Definitely a McGuffin.]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T18:55:40-08:00","id":369281,"title":"","content":"(Who says being a Mage is inherently superior to being a Changeling? Paradox <i>sucks.</i> But in character...)<br /> <br /> <i>Interesting...</i> I'd say that a valid price for that old thing would be a signature... oh, any on that tower in the center of the Hedge would do.<br /> <br /> Ah, but this... your innocence. How much would you pay to have <i>that</i> back?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T00:03:57-08:00","id":369532,"title":"","content":"I'd buy mine back with the skull of an honest man.<br /> <br /> <br /> I have an peculiar oddity for sale right here, a large hat that gobbles up it's wearer's shame when worn. (When worn the wearer cannot feel ashamed of anything that happens to themselves or anyone else.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T12:53:13-08:00","id":370038,"title":"","content":"The hat will sell for a meticulously detailed written autobiography of the buyer using the toilet.<br /> <br /> For sale: a plastic ice cube tray, two rows of eight cubes, currently full. Frozen in the centre of each cube is a spoken secret.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4722-birnam","name":"Birnam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T19:18:44-08:00","id":373222,"title":"","content":"(I have zero idea what's going on here, mind if I give this a try anyway?)<br /> <br /> For that? Well, I'd charge a bottle containing a truth that will truly break the listener's heart...<br /> <br /> How much would you give me for a &quot;Get out of jail free&quot; card, from a certain popular board game. This one, for reasons that sum up to &quot;The Wyrd&quot;, works on all prison institutions, even in the the Hedge or Arcadia?<br /> <br /> Of course, it's only good once...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T19:46:36-08:00","id":373234,"title":"","content":"I'll take that for a blasphemous truth. The more scandalous the info, the better.<br /> <br /> And here we have the first word ever spoken, long lost to time. It is the first proper word of any human language, buried among the annals of tomes, scrolls and tablets no longer readable. It is a word of great, ancient power, possibly Atlantean in origin, and the effects of speaking it are...surprising and random, to say the least. It is always, however, for the benefit of the speaker. (IG terms: roll a d100 whenever someone speaks the word. The higher the number, the more outrageous and insane an affect the ST has to come up with. The key here is that the affects cannot directly harm the speaker, but they help the speaker in some indirect way.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T21:33:19-08:00","id":373298,"title":"","content":"I'll take that for a $3 bill.<br /> <br /> A bit less rare than the last item, I'm selling this unique, one-of-a-kind piece of a Hedgespun. It looks like a dirty suit to you? Well, that's because its Mask and Mien have been <i>inverted</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T13:17:24-08:00","id":373706,"title":"","content":"A mirror owned by a vampire (if such things exist) can be exchanged for the suit.<br /> <br /> A rat that's somehow become hopelessly addicted to goblin fruit. It's kept in a wooden box and, when any goblin fruit is nearby, it will start to scratch and squeak to get out. When no fruit is present, it's perfectly tame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4722-birnam","name":"Birnam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T14:24:01-08:00","id":373790,"title":"","content":"For this poor rat, I would give a rabbit that dances when presented with a small piece of meat, even though he doesn't even eat it.<br /> <br /> Next up, a vinyl disc that seems to be indestructible and immune to the ravages of time. It contains the most popular songs played in Arcadia during the Victorian Era. They have no special characteristics other than being beautiful and very rare outside of Arcadia..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T15:59:27-08:00","id":373882,"title":"","content":"For that, my friend, I'd give a fiddle made by a group of exactly four &quot;Demons&quot;. <br /> <br /> Speaking of fakelore, how about this here rattlesnake. Like it? I got it off some cowboy who though himself a coyote. Doesn't seem like much... Except you can use him as a very special lasso. If you wrangle any element you have a contract with[Communion and Elements both work, as should certain Goblin Vows] from the smallest torches to a mighty hurricane, it'll become a potent steed that will take you to any one location, no matter how far, in exactly one day before returning to form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T16:15:38-08:00","id":373909,"title":"","content":"I'll give you a sock, rescued from a dryer that was really a portal to a volcano in the Hedge.<br /> <br /> And here, I present you pocket lint. Regular old pocket lint, except for one thing: it has been taken from an abandoned lab technician's coat inside the reactor at Chernobyl. Should you carry this lint in your pocket, you will be able to inflict radiation poisoning upon one foe per every cycle of the moon.... But at the cost of one of your loved ones suffering the same effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T21:16:48-08:00","id":374041,"title":"","content":"That sounds like it's worth this sheet of lead I have with me - two feet on a side, and one inch thick. <br /> <br /> But how about this fine find, ladies and gentlemen? A hat which is perfect for every situation. It's warm in the winter, cool and shading in the summer, and stylish with any outfit you might be wearing. Just don't wear it into battle, 'cuz it can't protect worth a damn and it's really fragile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T22:11:52-08:00","id":374054,"title":"","content":"For this Hat that is most perfect, I ask simply a trifle. Surreder to me the memory of your first childhood toy, and you may have this hat.<br /> <br /> But if you wouldn't be interested in that, I have here a sword. This sword is made of distilled moon metal quenched in the blood of a murderer. It is said that when held by a bloodstained hand, the wielder can feel the murderer's spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Wow I wish I had something cool to say here</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2227-dman1123","name":"dman1123","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-18T00:48:46-08:00","id":374108,"title":"","content":"...I'll give you an oak sapling which has never felt light.<br /> <br /> What about this book? It's a thick, mystical tome that details the strengths and weaknesses of every kith and court, as well as the basics of dream-weaving.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-18T05:26:46-08:00","id":374212,"title":"","content":"That is worth your own greatest weakness, bottled up and ready to use against you. <br /> <br /> Alternately, I'll just lure you to my Hollow, away from the protections of the Market, and kill you for it. I mean, seriously, showing that to a Winter Courtier? What did you think was going to happen?<br /> <br /> But here we have a handgun which has been fated never to kill. Wound, yes, and even severely - but none of its wounds will ever be fatal. What would that be worth to you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-18T11:58:13-08:00","id":374358,"title":"","content":"A weapon that doesn't kill... I should give you 7 hairs from the head of my worst enemy.<br /> <br /> And here I have armor, fated to save the wearers who deserves death the most. Please, tell me what you would give for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Wow I wish I had something cool to say here</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2227-dman1123","name":"dman1123","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-18T22:10:01-08:00","id":374876,"title":"","content":"I'll give eight human vertebrae: each is the second lumbar vertebrae from a different person that died in the last year.<br /> <br /> Next: a keyboard from, by appearance, an early 90's personal computer. Although it has the dimensions for a standard QWERTY setup, there is only one key in the centre of the plastic casing. It is simply labeled &quot;MEAT&quot;. There are no other indicators to its function.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4722-birnam","name":"Birnam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-18T23:28:56-08:00","id":374936,"title":"","content":"I'll give you a smashed screen; the cracks spell out the words &quot;WHAT IS WRITTEN ON TOWER BRIDGE?&quot;<br /> <br /> Ah, what's this? A complete tea-set, all made out of paper-thin human bone, and exquisitely painted with crushed coral and jade. My, just <i>look</i> at that brushwork! A perfect gift for the missus (or mister) in your life, don't you agree?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T00:49:18-08:00","id":374986,"title":"","content":"Paper-thin? I can beat that. I'll offer you this pair of scissors. You can run through anything but rock with these. I mean it! So long as you are running, you'll go right through.<br /> <br /> Now something for everyone: A bag which has, in fact, something for everyone. Sorry, no demonstrations--just the one something and I wouldn't want to waste mine on a demo. <b><u>No refunds.</u></b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4769-mjspra2","name":"mjspra2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T09:18:26-08:00","id":375309,"title":"","content":"What a coincidence! I have the perfect item to exchange for this bag: another bag, but it has something for no one. I found it inside a bottomless hole in a nameless cave of a godless realm. I showed part of it to an excessively curious mage and now he is a lot less nosy.<br /> <br /> Next up is a device bought from one of the Greys. It is a crystal cylinder holding a gelatinous, transparent hobgoblin. It can be fed with just about any organic material and it then produces eggs. When consumed, these eggs allow you to swap a number of dots from one Mental Attribute to another.equal to Wyrd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T06:59:36-08:00","id":421717,"title":"","content":"Well for that I can only offer this Jar of the light of Morn. Preserved and fresh as the day it was caught.<br /> <br /> What I offer now is a Venging Blade. It is a subtle knife with an edge that will cut steel. Bathe it in the blood of one whose life has been undone by another. From that day forth the knife will never cut nor draw blood from any but they that did the killing, and then will cut deeper and spark more pain than any blade ever wrought. You see, it was meant for none but the murderer. Such was the promise made in the blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}